.TH SYMMETRY 1
.SH NAME
symmetry \- mirror drawing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/symmetry
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Symmetry
is a mirror drawing, a port of the TempleOS symmetry demo.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Dragging button 2 rubber-bands a red mirror line and commits it on
release; releasing at the press point (a degenerate line) turns
symmetry off.
Dragging button 1 rubber-bands a straight black line, previewed
live together with its mirror image, and commits both on release.
A vertical mirror at the window's horizontal centre is active (but
not drawn) at startup.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B RMB drag
Set mirror line
.TP
.B LMB drag
Draw a straight line (mirrored)
.TP
.B Esc
Quit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/symmetry.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
